Package: tokr
Type: Package
Title: Process Models in the Plain-Text Language 'tok'
Version: 1.0.3
Authors@R: person("Marek", "Deja", email = "marek.deja@uj.edu.pl", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Reads, checks, formats and exports process models written in 'tok',
    a plain-text language for Business Process Model and Notation (BPMN) 2.0
    processes with their Decision Model and Notation (DMN) decisions, 'Camunda'
    forms and simulation parameters. Models are checked against the rules of
    BPMN 2.0, with diagnostics in English or Polish, and exported to BPMN files
    with a diagram layout, Scalable Vector Graphics (SVG) pictures, DMN and form
    files; they are drawn in the viewer and in 'R Markdown' and 'Quarto'
    documents through a 'knitr' engine. Processes are simulated as
    discrete-event models, giving indicators, an event log for process mining
    and a table of cases. The work is done by the 'Rust' engine of 'tok', shared
    with its 'Python' package and command line tool.
